cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Value-Field Theory (VFT)"
message: "If you use this theory or repository, please cite this repository."
authors:
  - family-names: "Nuno"
    given-names: "T."
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
abstract: >
  Value-Field Theory (VFT) is a structural framework for describing how
  multidimensional real resource and capital states K and nominal or expectation
  structures P across multiple actors form a value field whose attraction is
  realized through the actors' actions and decisions A. K, P, and A are not
  assumed to be scalar variables or probability distributions. At individual
  and local scales actions can often be observed directly, while at aggregate
  scales full action tracking is costly, so realized nominal change Delta P and
  realized real change Delta K can serve as principal proxies for aggregated
  action and flow. Aggregation, averaging, and distributional summaries are
  treated as analysis choices rather than core ontological assumptions.
repository-code: "https://github.com/nuno929/vf-model"
